          "score": 0.6434076,
          "snippet": "Two-dimensional semantics extends standard possible worlds frameworks to distinguish between epistemic and metaphysical necessity, thereby explaining how necessary truths can be known a priori. This approach relies on the Core Thesis that apriority corresponds to necessary first intensions, utilizing concepts like scrutability and PQTI sentences to ground conceptual analysis in metaphysics."
        },
        {
