          "snippet": "The text examines metaepistemological debates concerning the nature of epistemic facts, contrasting realist views that posit mind-independent truths with idealism and various forms of relativism. It argues that epistemic judgments may function prescriptively or express non-representational mental states rather than describing objective reality. Furthermore, it highlights tensions between orthodox epistemology and experimental results regarding knowledge attributions in contexts involving shifting stakes or environmental luck."
        },
        {
