          "title": "heidegger",
          "url": "https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/heidegger/",
          "score": 0.62561065,
          "snippet": "Heidegger argues that Western philosophy has forgotten the question of Being, necessitating a fundamental ontology grounded in Dasein's pre-ontological understanding. He characterizes human existence as being-in-the-world, defined by thrownness, projection, and being-with-others, while critiquing Cartesian subject-object dualism. Ultimately, his work seeks to uncover the temporal or event-based conditions that make intelligibility possible."
        },
